From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0420-amd-01-pr273.patch

Source: 0420-amd-01-pr273.patch
tree lacked

zortos293/Lichii PR 273 (68caa6c75e, zortos293, 6 Nov, "fix AMD shader typing, atomic retries and
compiler stalls") has four parts. Against this tree (local/T30, core 0001-0418 with white-03):

1. Compare-exchange loops retry with the word the exchange returned. CasLoop and the write-storage
   bitfield loop already do, under EDEN_NX2_CAS_RETURNED=1 (0397, sweep-01, from Lichii PR 206).
   The 8/16-bit shared store loop in DefineSharedMemory was the one loop left as it was; it now
   takes the same form under this switch. On AMD a plain reload can keep returning a stale copy,
   and the invocations that lost never match again: a hang or a lost device inside a compute
   program that packs bytes into shared memory, or wrong packed values.
2. Depth-compare samples keep a float image when the descriptor reads as an integer format:
   already in this tree (texture_pass.cpp, the sampled descriptor site), nothing to port.
3. Fragment shaders take the subgroup shuffle fallback (broadcast per lane) where the driver's
   fragment-stage shuffles are wrong. The PR sets it for AMD's Windows driver; the switch sets it
   on RADV too, as a test: fragment shaders run wave64 there, and a shuffle that crosses a guest
   warp's half would mix lanes of two pixels' quads (the fallback masks to the guest lane).
4. VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_DISABLE_OPTIMIZATION for two Ocarina compute shaders on AMD's Windows driver
   (6 and 18 minute compiles): driver-specific, not taken.

EDEN_NX2_AMD_PR273=1 turns on 1 and 3; unset, nothing changes (the AMD-Windows condition of 3
stays as upstream has it). Shaders are translated at every boot, so env.txt is enough. Clang
syntax check clean on emit_spirv_warp.cpp, spirv_emit_context.cpp and vk_pipeline_cache.cpp. Not
built, not run.
